WEBVTT

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:14.300
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:22.680
aoku nemuru mizu no hoshi ni sotto

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:22.680
Kissing softly the star of water that sleeps in blue,

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:31.410
kuchizuke shite inochi no hi wo tomosu hito yo

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:31.410
A person who lights the fire of life,

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:36.300
toki to iu kin'iro no sazanami wa

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:36.300
The time, the golden ripple,

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:45.070
oozora no kuchibiru ni umareta toiki ne

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:45.070
is a sigh from the lips of the sky,

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.300
kokoro ni uzumoreta

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.300
The stars of kindness...

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.270
yasashisa no hoshitachi ga

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.270
...buried in heart flame up...

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:56.440
honoo age yobiau

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:56.440
...and call to each other,

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:03.430
namima sasurau nanpasen no you ni

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:03.430
Like wrecked ships wandering on the waves...

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:08.870
mou nakanaide ima

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:08.870
Don't cry, any more,

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:16.240
anata wo sagashite iru hito ga iru kara

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:16.240
because now there is a person looking for you,

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.970
omae ni aitai yo to

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.970
Dying to see you...

00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:37.190
Jamaican enforced an outrageous plan
to drop a large colony.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:43.190
But, he offended Scirocco by doing so,
and the plan was leaked to the A.E.U.G..

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:47.700
Jamaican quickly retreated
without even getting reinforcements...

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:51.710
...and the day ended with the colony
not falling on Granada.

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:57.130
The Ghost of Zeon

00:01:57.920 --> 00:01:59.440
He took the beam rifle with him!

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:02.490
- Not the Vulcan?!
- What's the big deal?

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:05.550
It's got a blind spot, right beneath!
Are you aware of it?!

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:07.730
We've corrected the problem!

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:08.890
Lieutenant Yazan!

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:09.930
Yes, sir?

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:11.630
What's all this racket going on?

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:13.360
It's as if we were preparing for battle!

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:15.530
- That's my intention, sir.
- What?!

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:20.010
This ship is to return to Gryps at once
for supplies!

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:21.340
Yet you...!

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:23.740
That's why we must attack
the enemies...

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:25.610
...and stop them from
pursuing us.

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:28.080
When the heck did you suddenly become
our strategic advisor?!

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:32.320
Well, you could appoint me
to that position right now.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:34.250
Yazan, you bastard!

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:36.930
Do you have some sort of scheme in mind?

00:02:39.190 --> 00:02:42.160
- Terribly sorry, sir!
- Be careful, will you?!

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:44.330
All right, do as you wish.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:47.270
However, the Alexandria will not change
its planned course.

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:50.930
If I want to return, I'll do so on my own.

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:53.170
Don't forget what you just said.

00:02:53.810 --> 00:02:55.870
Thank you very much.

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:58.640
Your colony drop plan or my plan...

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:00.770
...I'll prove which one's better.

00:03:03.150 --> 00:03:04.590
Hurry with the armor check!

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:06.380
You guys are too damn slow!

00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:07.750
We're working on it!

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:09.290
- Getting used to things?
- Yes!

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:10.660
It's my second time.

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:13.520
Chief Petty Officer Adol.

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:14.930
Even if you detect the enemy...

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.690
...refrain from fighting
near their battleships!

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:17.560
Sir?

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:20.030
We'll drag the enemy here
to the Alexandria.

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:21.090
However...!

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:23.730
The reason we haven't been able
to sink the Argama to this point...

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:27.000
...is because we haven't been able to
effectively use this battleship's strengths.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.900
That's true!

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:30.810
I know.

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:35.480
And we must also teach Jamaican
the fears of fighting a battle!

00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:37.750
Squadron leader!

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:40.120
It's completely shrunk!
And we've not launched yet!

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:41.820
You can do better than that!

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.290
Oh, Lieutenant Emma.

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:51.330
How's the G-Defenser coming along?

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:53.460
It's ready to use.

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:55.260
In actual battle?

00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:57.270
We've done enough simulation tests.

00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:59.310
The rest is up to me.

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:02.530
I know you can do it, Lieutenant.

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:05.440
I'll send out the G-Defenser during
our next operation. What do you think?

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:07.780
Fine, sir.

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:10.480
I'll have them transfer it
to the mobile suit deck.

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:11.350
Lieutenant?

00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:13.920
Join me for a cup of tea?

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:15.920
No, sir.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:19.030
- He's got the timing all wrong.
- Exactly!

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:25.590
Adol! Don't fall behind!

00:04:25.670 --> 00:04:26.530
Okay!

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:44.350
We're not able to
catch up with the Dogosse Gier.

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:48.850
Judging from their actions, it looks
like the duties of the Dogosse Gier...

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:51.120
...are different from that of
other Titan battleships.

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:54.960
The Dogosse Gier is no
ordinary battleship.

00:04:55.030 --> 00:04:56.760
- What do you want?
- Oh.

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:59.730
I came to let you know that I'm done
prepping the Zeta Gundam.

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:01.460
What do you mean the Dogosse Gier
is not ordinary?!

00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:06.100
Well, I feel tremendous pressure
coming from that ship.

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:08.040
Is that so?

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:11.070
Lieutenant Quattro was saying
something similar to that.

00:05:11.150 --> 00:05:12.110
Yes.

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:14.810
Get some rest while you have the chance.

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:15.910
Yes, sir.

00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:17.840
- Hi!
- Hi.

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:21.420
He's become far more obedient.

00:05:21.490 --> 00:05:22.790
I don't need to talk to him, do I?

00:05:25.930 --> 00:05:27.830
It's following us around like a dog.

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:29.860
What an irritating battleship!

00:05:30.370 --> 00:05:32.060
<i>Shall we go, squadron leader?</i>

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:33.400
Proceed as we arranged.

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:35.330
We'll make them pay
for foiling our colony drop.

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:36.130
<i>Roger!</i>

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:41.280
Lieutenant?

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:44.100
Katz, how many times must I tell you?!

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:46.270
I'm also a full-fledged pilot!

00:05:46.350 --> 00:05:48.910
As things are, I don't know why
I'm assigned to the Radish.

00:05:48.980 --> 00:05:50.250
Don't get impatient.

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:53.510
It's not as if anyone's forgotten about you.

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:54.420
But...!

00:05:54.490 --> 00:05:56.320
We'll talk about that later.

00:05:56.390 --> 00:05:57.980
If only Lieutenant Quattro were here!

00:06:05.270 --> 00:06:08.100
If you let these bullets hit you,
it's coming out of your salary, Adol!

00:06:08.170 --> 00:06:09.870
I-I'll be more careful!

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:13.600
- Are you scared?
- I'm not at all scared!

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:15.910
In the battlefield, the ones who panic
end up dead!

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:18.240
- Remember that!
- Yes, sir.

00:06:18.980 --> 00:06:20.810
Gundam Mk. II! Taking off!

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:26.980
I'll lure the enemy away from the Radish!

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:29.820
There!

00:06:32.930 --> 00:06:34.230
Good. Full marks for bravery.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.020
It escaped?

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:43.690
Hey! What are you doing?!

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:47.110
We haven't received orders
for the G-Defenser to sortie!

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:51.010
Someone's got to take this
to the Mk. II, right?!

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:52.370
I'll do it!

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:54.850
What?! Who are you?!

00:06:55.050 --> 00:06:56.020
Hey!

00:06:56.720 --> 00:06:57.650
What did you say?!

00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:00.090
Katz is taking off in the G-Defenser
without orders?!

00:07:00.160 --> 00:07:02.490
Let him go!
It'll be a good lesson for him!

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:03.650
Will he be okay?

00:07:03.730 --> 00:07:05.320
He'll have Lieutenant Emma with him!

00:07:05.390 --> 00:07:06.190
Captain!

00:07:06.260 --> 00:07:08.230
Something's approaching us
from the right fore!

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:10.560
- It appears to be a battleship.
- What?!

00:07:12.270 --> 00:07:13.630
G-Defenser, taking off!

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:22.340
What?! It's coming straight at us?

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:23.670
Contact Yazan!

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:25.710
Can't do it! We're unable to connect to him!

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:28.310
What in the world is Yazan thinking?!

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:33.550
What?!

00:07:36.860 --> 00:07:38.220
Who's the pilot?

00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:41.020
- Are you that kid from the other day?
- You mean Kamille?

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:42.060
A woman?

00:07:59.780 --> 00:08:00.810
An old battleship?

00:08:03.990 --> 00:08:06.580
I have it! It's a Gwazine type
of the Principality of Zeon!

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:08.350
Zeon?

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:11.980
Where's the Mk. II?

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:18.960
Another new model?!

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:24.430
I need weapons!

00:08:26.710 --> 00:08:28.010
I'll try this!

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:32.670
A flare bomb?!

00:08:34.020 --> 00:08:35.110
What in the world?!

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:42.980
A battleship from yesteryear?!

00:08:43.060 --> 00:08:44.460
Over there!

00:08:45.930 --> 00:08:47.330
Miss Emma!

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:50.520
The G-Defenser?!

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:55.400
I'm not letting you!

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:05.710
A dream...!

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:13.720
No, that was no dream!

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:15.220
Miss Emma's in danger!

00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:19.030
I'm taking off! Requesting permission
to take off with the Zeta Gundam!

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:21.090
<i>What? Kamille?</i>

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:23.360
Miss Emma's in danger.
Please allow me to go.

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:24.920
<i>Wait! I'll transfer you to the captain!</i>

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:25.970
Kamille?

00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:28.270
Are you listening?

00:09:28.340 --> 00:09:29.890
What's this about Lieutenant Emma?!

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:30.700
<i>I can feel it!</i>

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:32.740
<i>Miss Emma is asking for help!</i>

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:34.700
The Radish is under attack?

00:09:35.210 --> 00:09:37.040
<i>Exactly! Please allow me to go!</i>

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:41.010
<i>Kamille's sensing something</i>
<i>that none of us can.</i>

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:42.380
<i>Captain Bright!</i>

00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:43.920
All right!
You can take off.

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:46.090
Thank you very much.

00:09:46.660 --> 00:09:48.620
He's very similar to Amuro Ray.

00:10:02.740 --> 00:10:04.200
Zeta Gundam, let's do it!

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:16.820
Can't do it! The timing's off!

00:10:17.390 --> 00:10:19.550
Miss Emma, what are you doing?!

00:10:23.190 --> 00:10:24.990
Things don't always work
as you'd like!

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:26.290
I'll shoot you down!

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:30.560
Damn you!

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:36.030
- Who is it?
- <i>Miss Emma! Escape from there!</i>

00:10:36.100 --> 00:10:37.070
Kamille?!

00:10:42.110 --> 00:10:43.600
It's the new model from the other day!

00:10:44.050 --> 00:10:45.980
You're back again
without a sign of regret!

00:10:50.020 --> 00:10:50.810
Take this!

00:10:57.390 --> 00:10:58.590
Miss Emma!

00:10:59.130 --> 00:10:59.920
Katz!

00:11:08.470 --> 00:11:09.770
The enemy...!

00:11:16.850 --> 00:11:18.400
Captain! It's the Zeta Gundam!

00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:19.910
The Zeta Gundam's here!

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:21.240
Are you sure?!

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:23.050
We've confirmed
its identification signal!

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:25.420
I'm pleased to see it.
I assume it's Kamille.

00:11:25.490 --> 00:11:26.420
Captain!

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:28.180
We're finished retrieving all the Nemos!

00:11:28.260 --> 00:11:30.490
Okay! We'll slowly move away.

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:31.920
Keep watching for enemies!

00:11:31.990 --> 00:11:33.650
It won't be
a phantom ship the next time!

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:41.800
Where's... the Mk. II?!

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:46.800
I've been found?!

00:11:50.780 --> 00:11:52.370
- It's here!
- You don't have the power!

00:11:54.720 --> 00:11:55.810
There's got to be...!

00:12:13.300 --> 00:12:14.270
Fall!

00:12:18.810 --> 00:12:20.780
W-Weapon! How about this?!

00:12:27.020 --> 00:12:28.680
I-I did it!

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:45.590
As if one backup unit
is going to make a difference!

00:12:55.240 --> 00:12:56.870
It's gone behind.

00:12:58.310 --> 00:12:59.370
Which way will it come from?

00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:06.720
Not bad, new model.

00:13:10.090 --> 00:13:13.720
He seems quite experienced in battle,
but I don't feel any mental pressure.

00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:15.320
He's just plain strong.

00:13:15.400 --> 00:13:16.730
However...!

00:13:24.210 --> 00:13:25.830
Am I stuck here?!

00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:34.440
The pilot's escaped!

00:13:38.120 --> 00:13:40.280
The G-Defenser's Core Fighter?

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:46.060
The Hizack's pilot.

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:47.990
Where's Katz?

00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:56.670
Nemo, look after the Mk. II for me.

00:13:57.010 --> 00:14:00.370
- I'm going down to rescue Katz.
- <i>Are you sure about this?</i>

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:03.470
You may have to take the Mk. II
and leave without me.

00:14:03.550 --> 00:14:04.510
<i>I understand.</i>

00:14:05.310 --> 00:14:07.610
If we let Katz die here...

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:11.050
...we'd wonder why we brought
him to space in the first place.

00:14:16.090 --> 00:14:19.250
The Radish will be out of the battle zone
in about one minute!

00:14:19.890 --> 00:14:21.760
We can't afford to let it escape!

00:14:21.830 --> 00:14:23.800
All gun platforms, begin firing at the ship!

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:28.130
But Lt. Commander, from here we'll
end up attacking the mobile suit battle area!

00:14:28.670 --> 00:14:30.330
Tell Yazan to take a detour!

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:31.600
He cannot be reached!

00:14:32.110 --> 00:14:34.730
Tch! I'm sure Yazan will find a way
to make it back on his own!

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:35.780
Fire!

00:14:39.610 --> 00:14:40.440
What?!

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:42.180
They're firing at us, their own people!

00:14:51.930 --> 00:14:52.890
Nothing.

00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:05.940
Who's there?

00:15:06.010 --> 00:15:06.970
Katz!

00:15:08.210 --> 00:15:09.180
Lieutenant Emma!

00:15:09.440 --> 00:15:11.380
What are you doing in a place like this?

00:15:11.450 --> 00:15:12.740
Looking for weapons!

00:15:12.810 --> 00:15:14.110
We must retreat!

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:17.240
There must be at least one mobile suit
in a ship of this size.

00:15:17.320 --> 00:15:19.150
- Forget about it, already!
- Watch out!

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:22.860
Must be the pilot from the Hizack
I saw above.

00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:34.430
We'll use that Gwazine as a shield
as we fire back at their ship!

00:15:34.500 --> 00:15:36.160
We'll fire as we ascend!

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:37.530
Don't hit that Gwazine!

00:15:43.480 --> 00:15:44.880
Out of power!

00:15:49.680 --> 00:15:51.050
I'm out of bullets!

00:16:04.930 --> 00:16:06.460
Hide-and-seek in mobile suits?!

00:16:25.320 --> 00:16:27.720
Will he come? Or is he waiting for me?

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:32.020
Katz!

00:16:42.040 --> 00:16:43.730
Hey, you over there! Throw your gun!

00:16:43.810 --> 00:16:46.170
- Lieutenant! Shoot!
- I'll shut you up, kid!

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:48.100
Stop!

00:16:54.750 --> 00:16:55.880
What the...?!

00:16:58.320 --> 00:16:59.650
Are you that Kamille guy?

00:16:59.720 --> 00:17:01.450
How do you know my name?!

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:05.110
The A.E.U.G.'s not much of an organization
to rely on women and children!

00:17:05.190 --> 00:17:07.420
It's the Titans that made it that way!

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:08.960
How dare you!

00:17:10.030 --> 00:17:10.930
Done already?

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:18.700
Where's the mobile suit you came on?

00:17:19.010 --> 00:17:20.670
I have an ally watching it.

00:17:20.740 --> 00:17:22.210
You won't be able to take it.

00:17:22.280 --> 00:17:24.610
I believe you.
I can't imagine you would just abandon it.

00:17:25.680 --> 00:17:27.170
Throw that vernier over here!

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:30.080
Not too used to actual battles,
are you, Chief Petty Officer.

00:17:30.490 --> 00:17:31.450
What?!

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:33.550
I wouldn't overdo it if I were you.

00:17:33.620 --> 00:17:35.320
All of us are afraid right now.

00:17:35.420 --> 00:17:37.720
Stop talking nonsense!
Hurry up!

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:43.800
Katz!

00:17:54.580 --> 00:17:55.540
Katz.

00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:06.140
Kamille?! What's he doing?!

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:14.420
The Zeta Gundam!

00:18:16.830 --> 00:18:17.820
There's someone there.

00:18:18.070 --> 00:18:19.030
Gotcha!

00:18:21.900 --> 00:18:22.670
Not yet!

00:18:27.310 --> 00:18:29.830
It's the same one as at the museum.

00:18:29.910 --> 00:18:31.210
Will it move?

00:18:32.110 --> 00:18:33.380
Of course not.

00:18:43.160 --> 00:18:43.850
What?!

00:18:46.760 --> 00:18:47.960
This is it!

00:18:51.070 --> 00:18:53.470
How dare you!
But I've got one more arm!

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:03.510
I can use this!

00:19:03.580 --> 00:19:04.670
That won't help you!

00:19:13.520 --> 00:19:14.490
Katz!

00:19:19.330 --> 00:19:20.390
Lieutenant Emma!

00:19:20.460 --> 00:19:23.060
Kamille, go after the enemy!
Katz is all right.

00:19:23.130 --> 00:19:24.790
- But...!
- Go!

00:19:25.230 --> 00:19:26.720
Okay!

00:19:28.970 --> 00:19:30.270
Come on, Katz.

00:19:30.340 --> 00:19:32.500
- We're getting out of here!
- R-Right!

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:38.510
I'm not about to let things end like this.

00:19:41.920 --> 00:19:43.440
That's what I like to see.

00:19:43.520 --> 00:19:45.540
I'm glad you caught up.

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:47.750
Why were you waiting?

00:19:48.020 --> 00:19:49.990
I was worried about both you and Katz!

00:19:50.360 --> 00:19:51.150
Lieutenant!

00:19:53.130 --> 00:19:54.420
Lieutenant Commander Jamaican!

00:19:54.500 --> 00:19:57.830
That bastard! Bragging his head off,
only to run back to us!

00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:04.360
- He stopped!
- This is our chance!

00:20:04.440 --> 00:20:05.410
Be quiet!

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:08.640
This is all because you took off
unnecessarily!

00:20:08.710 --> 00:20:10.070
Enemy mobile suit detected!

00:20:10.140 --> 00:20:12.270
Gun platforms, get ready for counterattack!

00:20:13.010 --> 00:20:15.740
Fire, Gundam! Don't miss your target.

00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:17.990
Miss Emma!

00:20:32.870 --> 00:20:34.100
This is a battlefield, after all.

00:20:42.310 --> 00:20:44.180
Kamille, I'm sorry.

00:20:44.250 --> 00:20:47.440
I lost my temper because you pay
too much attention to saving allies...

00:20:47.520 --> 00:20:48.810
...even in the heat of battle.

00:20:49.150 --> 00:20:50.120
No.

00:20:50.320 --> 00:20:52.290
What you said was correct, Lieutenant.

00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:55.320
I'll concentrate more on the fight itself.

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:57.750
Katz, thanks.
You saved my life.

00:20:58.690 --> 00:21:00.660
<i>I would've been defeated</i>
<i>if you weren't there.</i>

00:21:00.730 --> 00:21:03.200
But you're going to scold me
despite your words.

00:21:03.830 --> 00:21:06.300
That's not our job.

00:21:06.730 --> 00:21:09.530
Be prepared for a lecture
from Captain Henken.

00:21:19.410 --> 00:21:21.470
So it <i>is</i> A Baoa Qu and Gryps.

00:21:22.150 --> 00:21:24.850
Yes, but it's an analytical diagram
the computer came up with...

00:21:24.920 --> 00:21:26.680
...so I can't be sure how accurate it is.

00:21:26.750 --> 00:21:28.650
No, there's no mistake about it.

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:32.090
I heard about former
Principality of Zeon guys...

00:21:32.160 --> 00:21:35.130
...joining forces with the Titans
to build a space fortress.

00:21:35.700 --> 00:21:38.670
So, that's in this area ahead of us.

00:21:45.870 --> 00:21:48.100
Good job.
I thank you, Kamille.

00:21:48.580 --> 00:21:50.840
No, the credit goes to Katz.

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:52.850
He did great to save me.

00:21:54.620 --> 00:21:57.910
This time around, I sent you out
to test the G-Defenser, as well.

00:21:58.320 --> 00:22:01.250
But next time you take off on your own,
I'm sending you to the brig.

00:22:01.320 --> 00:22:02.580
- Got that?
- Yes, sir.

00:22:03.360 --> 00:22:04.190
Kamille.

00:22:04.260 --> 00:22:06.390
We have word from the Argama...

00:22:06.460 --> 00:22:08.390
...that Lieutenant Quattro's
returning from Earth.

00:22:08.460 --> 00:22:09.490
Really?

00:22:09.560 --> 00:22:11.220
The Argama's going to pick him up.

00:22:11.300 --> 00:22:12.530
That Gwazine's going down.

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:45.730 --> 00:23:50.660
The Argama must remain in satellite orbit
in order to retrieve Char's shuttle.

00:23:51.030 --> 00:23:53.660
At this time, Jerid, Mouar,
and Sarah approach...

00:23:53.730 --> 00:23:56.930
...equipped with the powerful
Mega Launcher.

00:23:57.540 --> 00:23:59.030
During the defensive battle...

00:23:59.110 --> 00:24:01.840
...Kamille senses
the calm eye of an enemy.

00:24:02.710 --> 00:24:07.010
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"Rendezvous with Char".

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:12.440
Next Episode

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:12.440
Rendezvous with Char

00:24:07.850 --> 00:24:10.550
You will see the tears of time.
